1
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,630
Hey!

2
00:00:12,713 --> 00:00:14,437
You won't find a better deal, signore!

3
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,377
The other guy said the same thing.

4
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:18,757
I'll throw in a personal tour of the city.

5
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:19,670
Huh?

6
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:20,583
Seriously?

7
00:00:20,666 --> 00:00:21,640
What a character! What?

8
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:22,801
Where did it go?

9
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:23,810
What's wrong?

10
00:00:23,893 --> 00:00:26,980
My back disappeared!
Huh? As agreed. So then?

11
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:28,717
Is there anything I should know about?

12
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,630
Not a thing.

13
00:00:29,713 --> 00:00:30,900
Thanks to you.

14
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:32,040
Is that right?

15
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:33,540
I'll be off then.

16
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:37,544
This is what you wanted, right?

17
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,013
Yeah, that's the stuff.

18
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:42,357
But the thing is, this is all the
money I could scrounge together.

19
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,911
In that case, I guess this is all you get.

20
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,800
The Jewel of Southern Italy, Napoli.

21
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:02,940
It's a city so beautiful, a single
visit can satisfy the soul unto death.

22
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:04,434
Or so the saying goes.

23
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:06,440
Excuse me!

24
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:10,157
Do you know how we can get to
the Church of Santa Chiara?

25
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:12,340
Oh, Santa Chiara, you say?

26
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,297
You're going to want to keep straight.

27
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,217
Then at the first signal, you...

28
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,500
I knew it!

29
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,000
The Church is that way!

30
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,398
Okay, you're right!

31
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,580
Thank you very much for your help!

32
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:23,214
Are you alright, miss?

33
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:24,130
Oh, yeah.

34
00:01:24,213 --> 00:01:25,473
Thanks for catching me.

35
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,348
Sorry for bumping into you.

36
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:30,373
Just watch where you're going next time.

37
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,800
Let's take off. Hey, miss.

38
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:40,008
You must have dropped this.

39
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:41,150
No way!

40
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,940
Oh, my gosh, you're the best!

41
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,020
Happy to help.

42
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:47,120
Wow, talk about Mr.

43
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:48,277
Sweep you off your feet.

44
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,831
I should have snuck a pig with that cutie.

45
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:52,770
Bizarre.

46
00:01:52,853 --> 00:01:54,482
Did they just fly out of my bag?

47
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:56,617
I thought they landed there and flew off.

48
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:57,700
Probably right.

49
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,900
Here in Napoli, vigilance
is a prized virtue.

50
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:14,600
Excuse me, I'll take a
chocolado and pistachio, please.

51
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:17,210
Huh?

52
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:19,940
Make it two. Va bene.

53
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:40,100
Come on, people!

54
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:41,700
No license, no work!

55
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,177
Don't make me say it again!

56
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:44,780
Get a move on, would ya?

57
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,940
Cut, so. Hey!

58
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:48,940
You only moved one time down!

59
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:49,950
There, you see?

60
00:02:50,033 --> 00:02:50,863
A mess.

61
00:02:50,946 --> 00:02:51,776
I can bypass that.

62
00:02:51,859 --> 00:02:52,689
What do you think?

63
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,357
They're in a cheaper way downtown. Yeah.

64
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,270
Yeah?

65
00:02:56,353 --> 00:02:57,183
What do you call cheap?

66
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,190
Luca!

67
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,340
Did you forget?

68
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:10,560
You fork over the street tax you
owe me before doing business.

69
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,040
Mercy, please!

70
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,057
I thought I was pretty clear.

71
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:16,517
Taxes first, then work. But...

72
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,680
But what, Ted man?

73
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,725
But I've got a family to feed.

74
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:21,530
Oh.

75
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:29,140
Please, no!

76
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:33,517
I'd like to say I feel for you, guy,
but friendship is thicker than blood.

77
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,430
Got it?

78
00:03:34,513 --> 00:03:38,360
If you want me, you won't know who
else is dealing behind your back!

79
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:40,650
Name.

80
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:43,620
Give me the rat bastard's name.

81
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,280
It's Giorno!

82
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:46,780
Giorno Giovanna!

83
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,430
Giorno?

84
00:03:48,513 --> 00:03:51,067
Yeah, and the kid's been
making a killer too!

85
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,640
So that's how it is.

86
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:56,530
Thanks.

87
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,440
The info's much appreciated.

88
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,560
Hey, Buster!

89
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,237
Did you hear what I just said?

90
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,880
No license, no work!

91
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,440
Keep it moving! Buongiorno!

92
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,640
I finally made it.

93
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,660
What a journey.

94
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:20,640
I'm definitely not in Japan anymore.

95
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,061
Okay, let's get down to business.

96
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,241
Haruno Shiobana.

97
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:27,417
That's not a name you hear every day.

98
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,037
I should head for the hotel.

99
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:32,649
I can't track this guy down
carrying my bags around with me.

100
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:36,780
All right, now to find a taxi
stand. Damn! Look at him go!

101
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,977
I know, I can't think of anyone who
can futz with their ear like that.

102
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:42,884
It's one hell of a crazy trick.

103
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,700
How is he even doing that?

104
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,860
Gross! That's foul.

105
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:50,840
How'd this guy fold in
his entire ear? Wow.

106
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:53,848
Gotta say, kid, that
just made my whole day.

107
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:55,090
Crazy.

108
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,477
Just keep it on the down low, yeah?

109
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,680
You stay weird now.

110
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:03,940
Need a taxi?

111
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,117
No, no, I'm fine, really, thank you.

112
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,030
Are you sure?

113
00:05:07,113 --> 00:05:09,260
I'll drop you off for 180,000 lira.

114
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:10,617
That's a pretty sweet deal.

115
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:13,177
And I can at least get
you to the center of town.

116
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:14,200
Let's see now.

117
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:18,257
So the conversion would be about
10,000 yen. Not interested.

118
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:20,458
That's double the going rate, buddy!

119
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:22,220
Wow, nice job.

120
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,017
You speak excellent Italian.

121
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:24,930
Huh?

122
00:05:25,013 --> 00:05:26,277
Have you ever lived here in Italy?

123
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,557
Oh, no, I just had my friend
Rohan sensei make it so...

124
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,417
N-never mind that, it's not important.

125
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,737
So, are you really willing
to drive me to town?

126
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:37,217
I mean, you look like you're in junior
high or high school at the very most.

127
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,617
And what exactly was that
thing you handed to the guard?

128
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:41,117
I'm pretty sure I saw cash.

129
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:42,117
Did you pay them off?

130
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,657
No, it's nothing like that.

131
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,837
Don't bust a gasket.

132
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:47,677
So, 10,000 lira then, and forget the tip.

133
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:49,857
Let's get going before it gets late.

134
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:53,300
Wait, isn't 10,000 lira 500 yen?

135
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,500
Uh, that won't be necessary.

136
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,800
I'll just wait like everyone else.

137
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:00,998
Still want to wait?

138
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:04,980
10,000, you said? That's right.

139
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:08,217
Trade-off is you have to
carry your own luggage.

140
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:10,182
You don't have to tip, remember?

141
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:15,349
Bags up front, you're taking
the luxury spot, the back seat.

142
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:18,237
I should warn you in advance.

143
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:22,797
I'm not some naive Japanese tourist, so
you'd better not try anything funny, got it?

144
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,645
I expect this car to head
straight to my hotel.

145
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:28,924
Certo, you want me to go
straight to your hotel.

146
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:33,595
Sounds good, though your bags
will be empty on arrival.

147
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,000
What the? He left?

148
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:39,557
Why would he take off
before I could get in?

149
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:41,157
Hey, pretend you didn't see.

150
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,460
Shit, no, no, no, come back.

151
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,040
Ciao for now.

152
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:46,639
Reverb, act three!

153
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:58,120
It didn't have to end this way.

154
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:02,300
I told you, don't try
to pull anything funny.

155
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:05,277
I'm not gonna stop you from running.

156
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:08,301
Once I grab my belongings,
we'll be all done here.

157
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,660
Look at him go!

158
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,797
Giorno must have botched the job!

159
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:20,177
What did the kid expect scamming a Japanese
tourist when he's half Japanese himself?

160
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:23,557
But with that hair color and
a name like Giorno Giovanna,

161
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:26,937
who'd ever guess he doesn't have
a drop of Italian blood in him?

162
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:28,420
There's no way...

163
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:32,470
What?

164
00:07:32,553 --> 00:07:33,800
It's all gone! How?

165
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,901
It's like some kind of weird egg.

166
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,820
Is this thing a stand?

167
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:50,413
Why would one show up the
moment I touched down in Italy?

168
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:55,137
I must have been out of my mind.

169
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:58,117
That's not a stand, it's
a living, breathing thing.

170
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:01,117
Creepy tree frog aside, how'd
my suitcase just disappear?

171
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,977
There's no way he could
have hidden it that fast.

172
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,100
Uh, what's happening?

173
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:09,246
I've got to get some answers.

174
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:11,100
Uh, Scusi?

175
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:14,425
Can you tell me anything
about that cab driver?

176
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,520
Any minute now.

177
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:28,960
You're Giorno Giovanna, right?

178
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,960
We haven't met before, have we?

179
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:39,080
Giorno, you have any clue who I am?

180
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:40,600
Leaky Eye Luca.

181
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:44,417
You were in a dispute a while
back, and when it turned ugly,

182
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:48,237
you took a knife to the face, but kept
fighting and swinging to spite your wound.

183
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:52,257
The complications from that little scrap
left you with a perpetually leaking eye,

184
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:53,458
hence your moniker.

185
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:58,679
Here, take a load off and
make yourself comfortable.

186
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,237
What's the holdup? Pop a squat.

187
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:07,737
looking up at you is
hurting my eyes so how old

188
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:12,677
are you 15 and change
what really haha you're a

189
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,777
baby so here's the thing
Giorno any true friendship

190
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:19,077
has to be built on the
firm foundation of the

191
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,637
three T's you've heard
of them haven't you in

192
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:24,137
case you're drawing a blank
the first one is truth

193
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:27,737
the second one is tolerance
last but not least you

194
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:31,357
have the third T tribute
and voila the three T's

195
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:34,557
of true friendship was
there something you needed

196
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:37,357
I wasn't finished showing
you the rope so shut

197
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,717
your face hole nobody said
you could ask questions

198
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:43,397
drones all as for what I
needed I hear you started

199
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:46,837
a hustle at the airport
huh surely you can see

200
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:49,237
how this would be
confusing after all I don't

201
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,377
remember receiving any
tribute from you and without

202
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:56,340
tribute how could we remain
true friends now hand

203
00:09:56,860 --> 00:09:57,717
over your wallet.

204
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,660
Signore, you've got it wrong.

205
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,257
I've already paid your tribute.

206
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,477
I don't have any money.

207
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,157
You talking about that, guard?

208
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,757
You have to be a special kind of stupid
to think I'm working with that old...

209
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,670
Huh?

210
00:10:08,753 --> 00:10:09,854
What the hell is this?

211
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:10,940
A family photo?

212
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:13,302
I know you're holding out on me,

213
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:16,137
so fork over the cash right now, blondie.

214
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:19,380
Signore Luca, I really hate
having to repeat myself.

215
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:23,320
And as I've already said, I
don't owe you anything. Huh?

216
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:26,347
Now please don't make
me say it a third time.

217
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,080
Test to the castle!

218
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,180
Time out, kid.

219
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:36,754
What the hell is that?

220
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:39,760
So he came back. Flick it off!

221
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:42,757
No, the frog has nothing to do with this.

222
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,437
Please don't ask me to do that.

223
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,932
That wasn't a freaking suggestion, Amiko!

224
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:49,297
And you still haven't
paid the taxes you owe!

225
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:51,897
Are you seriously gonna
refuse both of my orders?

226
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:53,917
You've got some brass balls, kid!

227
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,353
No one says no to leaky-eyed Luka twice!

228
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:59,497
This frog is a living creature
with a will of his own.

229
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,397
He thinks and acts for himself.

230
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:03,068
Let's go our separate ways.

231
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,070
You're really starting to piss me off.

232
00:11:04,153 --> 00:11:05,757
Flicking him off is
something I just can't do.

233
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:08,580
Just shut your damn mouth already! Stop!

234
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,377
He's harmless if you leave him alone!

235
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:12,960
Get ready to die, you insubordinate dick!

236
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,177
Don't say I didn't try to warn you.

237
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:26,731
This little guy here isn't totally loyal
to me, as you're about to find out.

238
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,377
Just remember, he's
only protecting himself,

239
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:32,636
as anyone would protect
something as precious as life.

240
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,720
Do you get it now?

241
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:44,040
An attack on him is an attack
on oneself, and a fatal one.

242
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,357
But bear this in mind,

243
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:50,560
I asked you very nicely not to
make me repeat myself a third time.

244
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:52,980
Repeating oneself is futile.

245
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:57,020
It's a big waste of time,
and a bigger waste of breath.

246
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:58,960
Totally useless.

247
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:08,185
You want me to get a skin
sample from this kid?

248
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:09,470
That's right.

249
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:11,995
Send it to me as soon as it's secured.

250
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:15,492
The Speedwagon Foundation will
examine his genetic makeup.

251
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:16,760
His DNA?

252
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:18,497
What's so special about him?

253
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:22,820
Let's just say that his dead father
was unique, hence the analysis.

254
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,837
I don't need much to begin.

255
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,861
An epidermal sample will suffice.

256
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,278
That's the rundown.

257
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:32,680
I'll cover your travel expenses. What?

258
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,271
You're covering them all?

259
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:36,440
That's sort of eerie.

260
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:42,320
About this kid, not to sound weird, but he
bears a really strong resemblance to you.

261
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:49,222
The address written on this photo
should be around here somewhere.

262
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:51,613
They should watch that.

263
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:54,397
There's no reason for you to be concerned.

264
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:57,597
No one around here would be
foolish enough to steal their bag.

265
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,268
Not if they wanted to live.

266
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,460
Wow, that's impressive.

267
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,839
This area must be pretty safe, huh?

268
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:08,937
Signore, how about some lunch?

269
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:10,677
Thanks for the offer, but I'll pass.

270
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:11,757
Don't you want to drink with me?

271
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,057
I promise you won't regret it.

272
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:13,970
I'll pay for it.

273
00:13:14,053 --> 00:13:14,883
How about no?

274
00:13:14,966 --> 00:13:15,796
Can I come?

275
00:13:15,879 --> 00:13:18,500
Now all of you just go
away and leave me be. Okay.

276
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:21,900
Ademani journal. Ciao now.

277
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,731
It's the guy from before!

278
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:27,490
Huh?

279
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:30,640
I finally found you, you lousy crook!

280
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:32,197
That's my money you got!

281
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:33,110
You!

282
00:13:33,193 --> 00:13:34,023
How'd you know I was here?

283
00:13:34,106 --> 00:13:37,397
Where the heck is my passport
and what did you do with my bags?

284
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:41,117
It really pains me to have to tell
you this, But your stuff is gone.

285
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,030
I sold it.

286
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:42,943
Sorry, Amiko.

287
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,740
Now you know, so stop chasing me.

288
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:48,680
You're not getting away again!

289
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:50,626
What's weighing down my hand?

290
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:54,040
So earlier, that wasn't
the car malfunctioning?

291
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:58,100
This stranger, could he have
the same kind of powers as me?

292
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:00,665
Hang on, what did he just say?

293
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,640
Golden wind!

294
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:09,650
End!

295
00:14:09,733 --> 00:14:10,968
Plant the seed of vitality.

296
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,280
Bring forth new life.

297
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,717
There was something there, I'm sure of it.

298
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,820
Act three, go!

299
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:24,340
The target has vanished. Damn that guy.

300
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:28,914
How'd he manage to break free from
three freezes pressure grip so easily?

301
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:33,017
I'll say it again.

302
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,900
I strongly suggest you
abandon following me.

303
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:39,944
I despise saying something a second
time when once is sufficient.

304
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:43,340
Repetition is the very
essence of futility.

305
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,877
Some friendly advice for you, stranger.

306
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,784
Try not to lead a useless life.

307
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:51,126
Take him down, Act Three,
before he gets away!

308
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:59,200
The force ricocheted back to me
when I hit the tree, but why?

309
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,127
I stole all your belongings.

310
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:05,517
Yet you still held back
when you attacked me.

311
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:09,012
Your injuries tell me everything
I need to know about you.

312
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,640
You, Amiko, have a good soul.

313
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,640
There's no doubt about it.

314
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,680
Giorno Giovanna.

315
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:21,080
That kid is a stand user.

316
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:38,790
Hello.

317
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,440
Jotaro, it's Koichi.

318
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:42,580
Ah, good to hear from you.

319
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:45,180
Did you make it to Italy? I found him.

320
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:46,897
The kid you asked me to look into.

321
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:47,960
Haruno Shibana.

322
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:49,940
That was record time.

323
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,677
Yeah, well I hope you're
holding onto your hat.

324
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,525
I ran into him at the airport.

325
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,480
And we kind of had it out.

326
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:58,377
But now we have confirmation.

327
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:00,497
He's a stand user and a strong one.

328
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:02,580
He goes by Giorno Giovanna here.

329
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,497
It's just like you said, Mr.

330
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:05,410
Jotaro.

331
00:16:05,493 --> 00:16:07,948
Stand users are somehow
drawn to each other.

332
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:10,276
Our meeting was completely by chance.

333
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:13,697
He looks like a student, but acts
like he's in some sort of gang.

334
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:15,721
He stole my bag and all my money.

335
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,317
And then there's his stand ability.

336
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:21,757
Seems like he can reflect attacks
right back at the attacker.

337
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,617
I'm sorry about all the trouble.

338
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,517
I'll get you a room and some money.

339
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,517
Just hang tight.

340
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:27,430
Thank you, Mr.

341
00:16:27,513 --> 00:16:28,343
Jotaro.

342
00:16:28,426 --> 00:16:29,297
Oh, and the picture's outdated.

343
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,321
He's blonde now.

344
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:34,317
I spoke to some people who know him,
and they said he didn't dye his hair.

345
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,760
It just changed, and recently, too.

346
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:39,097
This is probably a sensitive subject,

347
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:42,298
but you mentioned his father
when I started all this.

348
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:43,610
Mr.

349
00:16:43,693 --> 00:16:45,498
Jotaro, are you two related somehow?

350
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,280
His father and I go way back.

351
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,708
I'm the one who killed him.

352
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,960
His name was Dio Brando.

353
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,060
Did you say Dio?

354
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,740
As in the bow and arrow, Dio?

355
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:02,860
The very one.

356
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:06,337
I learned this year that Dio
may have fathered a child.

357
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:08,280
I needed to uncover the truth.

358
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:12,780
I had to know whether Giorno Giovanna
was Dio's son, and if he was,

359
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
how much he took after his father.

360
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:18,340
But didn't Dio's body
once belong to a Joestar?

361
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,660
You said he has blonde hair now.

362
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:22,140
Be careful.

363
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:26,877
That may be proof that Dio's blood has
only recently awakened his stand power.

364
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,901
Something must have triggered it.

365
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:33,002
There's a good chance a powerful
stand user has arrived in Naples.

366
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,300
Man, just what we didn't need.

367
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:39,657
You've been through enough already,
so keep your distance from this kid.

368
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:40,570
Got it?

369
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:44,480
One last thing.

370
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:47,020
Do you think he's a true enemy?

371
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:49,654
More to the point, could he be an ally?

372
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,800
What does your gut say?

373
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,380
You're the only one who's met him.

374
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,815
How'd he come across?

375
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:02,297
I can't say for sure, but there was a...

376
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:03,760
How do I put this?

377
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,860
He had a certain eloquence about him.

378
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:25,680
Is this yours? It's not.

379
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:27,320
Hmm, I see.

380
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,680
It's my lucky day.

381
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:35,200
Tell me, if you were to
find a bag on this tram,

382
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:38,991
a bag that had a billion lira
inside, would you turn it in?

383
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,177
You're joking, right?

384
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:42,560
It's finder's keepers.

385
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,313
At least you're honest.

386
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:49,618
But what if I was really an undercover
cop, and I saw the whole thing?

387
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:51,650
Ah,

388
00:18:51,733 --> 00:18:55,597
well in that case, I'd let you mosey off
with half the money to look the other way.

389
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:56,510
Probably.

390
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,380
Now that's the spirit.

391
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,337
And you know, I get the
sense you really would.

392
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:07,497
The look on your face isn't the
expression of a bluffing man.

393
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,277
I can clearly see that
you're telling the truth.

394
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:14,457
You see, I have a special knack for
telling whether someone's being truthful.

395
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:16,422
And I don't often make mistakes.

396
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:19,977
Have you ever noticed how the
face often glistens with sweat?

397
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,884
That's normally the first tell.

398
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:24,417
But what's important
is the sweat's flavor.

399
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,971
That's the telltale sign.

400
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:30,440
Chichou, who exactly are you?

401
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:34,517
Leaky Iluca got his head bashed
in with his own shovel and was

402
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:37,757
conveniently found unconscious
on the outskirts of the airport.

403
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:41,017
He's critical and it's looking
like he's never going to come too.

404
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:43,677
And I've come here to
hunt down the culprit.

405
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:44,860
So let's talk.

406
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:49,418
No one has the slightest idea why
Leaky Iluca was even at the airport.

407
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:51,290
However,

408
00:19:51,373 --> 00:19:53,697
I spoke with a security
guard and was told that

409
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:56,368
a young man named Giorno
Giovanna was there.

410
00:19:56,500 --> 00:20:00,577
If it's not too much trouble, I thought
we'd have a quick chat about the matter.

411
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:01,490
Chat, huh?

412
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:02,660
You a cop or what?

413
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:03,936
Don't be ridiculous.

414
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:07,015
Luca wasn't some ordinary street punk.

415
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:10,677
He was a mafioso, and several
people had reason to off him.

416
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:13,054
He had a special knack for being hated.

417
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:17,857
Problem is, that's not how his boss
is electing to see the situation.

418
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:20,577
A member of the Familia has been slain,

419
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:23,657
and what honor he had has
been severely compromised.

420
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:25,557
He's ordered me to find the perpetrator,

421
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:28,057
and sort out everything
surrounding this mess.

422
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:29,846
Make this easy and cooperate.

423
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:31,390
Understand?

424
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:35,380
Did you meet up with Leaky
Ailuka at the airport? Leaky who?

425
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,718
Never heard of him.

426
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:49,440
You're not perspiring.

427
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,865
Right then, that's all I need.

428
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,296
You're in the clear.

429
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,320
Sorry to bother you, Giorno Giovanna.

430
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:11,760
What the hell is going on?

431
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:14,080
And why was my fist clenched?

432
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:16,257
You're looking at Luca's right eye.

433
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:19,811
It's not currently in use, so
I thought I'd bring it along.

434
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,700
What a surprise.

435
00:21:23,180 --> 00:21:25,239
That's the distinct tang of a liar.

436
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:26,740
Right, Giorno Giovanna?

437
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,200
I have to apologize.

438
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:35,782
I know I said we were done with questions,
but it seems the game has changed a bit.

439
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:37,740
Wouldn't you agree, Giorno?

440
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:42,040
I now know you're a liar,
but the question is why.

441
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,720
Don't be shy, Amico.

442
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:48,431
I'm really very interested in
hearing what you have to say.

443
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:51,996
What's with you all?

444
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:53,397
Jealous or something?

445
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,340
I'll gladly let you in on this.

446
00:21:57,640 --> 00:22:00,017
You can call me Bruno Bucciarati.

447
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:01,218
Time for the truth.

448
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:04,618
We've already progressed
from questioning to torture.

449
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:14,960
well what do you think terrifying trick
isn't it are those they're luca's fingers

450
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:19,797
my turn to confess luca bit
the big one courtesy of our

451
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:24,057
aforementioned boss he didn't see
the use in keeping dead weight around

452
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:29,817
his fingers not again what did
he do damn it could he have

453
00:22:29,900 --> 00:22:33,937
powers like that japanese tourist
oh and i'm not just a human lie

454
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:38,097
detector i have other tricks up
my sleeve as you've just seen for

455
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:42,237
yourself i can fit almost anything
inside your mouth for example

456
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:45,877
it'd be child's play to slide
that extinguisher between your

457
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:50,440
jaws of course if i did you'd be
joining Luca in the afterlife.

458
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:56,000
Now talk!

459
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,860
You know exactly who attacked Luca.

460
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:01,080
Were you paid to keep quiet?

461
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:03,277
Although I suppose it
doesn't really matter.

462
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:05,772
You'll still tell me what I want to know.

463
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:08,557
I guess that answers my question.

464
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:10,111
He definitely has powers.

465
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:14,202
You will tell me everything, or
the torture is going to intensify.

466
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,680
Jo no Jabaya!

467
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,800
This guy's deadly!

468
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:25,540
There's no other way.

469
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:30,377
If I want a chance in hell
at winning this fight,

470
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:32,636
I'm going to have to use Golden Wind!

471
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:55,350
Thank you.
